# Citation metadata for SteinerMineBench.
#
# The dataset DOI is minted by Zenodo when a release is tagged on GitHub. Until
# then the `doi:` key below is absent rather than a dummy value, so this file is
# always valid CFF. After minting, add the CONCEPT DOI (the version-independent
# one, not the per-version DOI) as:
#
#     doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
#
# The paper is in preparation; fill in `journal` and add `doi` to the
# preferred-citation block once it is published. Editing Zenodo record metadata
# after minting does not change the DOI.
#
# `python validate.py --publication` re-checks that no unfilled template markers
# have crept back into this file, .zenodo.json or the README.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SteinerMineBench, please cite the dataset. Once the accompanying paper is published, please cite both."
type: dataset

title: "SteinerMineBench: a benchmark suite for geotechnically-weighted Steiner trees on voxel grids"
abstract: >-
  Twenty-four synthetic, procedurally generated benchmark instances for
  underground mine ramp network optimisation, modelled as directed Steiner
  arborescences on three-dimensional voxel cost grids derived from the NGI
  Barton Q-system. Instances vary along four controlled axes: fault
  architecture crossed with rock mass quality regime, portal location,
  production zone count, and voxel resolution from 1.3e5 to 1.3e8 voxels. Each
  bundle ships a compressed cost grid, complete metadata, a reference solution
  labelled exact or best-known, and a provably valid lower bound, so that other
  researchers can run their own solvers on identical instances and report an
  optimality gap. All data is synthetic and is not derived from any operating
  mine.

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"

repository-code: "https://github.com/1NightCrawler2/SteinerMineBench"
url: "https://github.com/1NightCrawler2/SteinerMineBench"

authors:
  - family-names: "Hasozdemir"
    given-names: "Kursat"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2710-9562"
    affiliation: "Department of Mining Engineering, Istanbul Technical University"
    email: "hasozdemir@itu.edu.tr"

keywords:
  - mine planning
  - underground mining
  - ramp network design
  - Steiner tree
  - directed Steiner arborescence
  - voxel model
  - Barton Q-system
  - rock mass classification
  - geotechnical engineering
  - combinatorial optimisation
  - benchmark dataset

